don't have the data?

703
00:37:57,410 --> 00:38:02,300
PROFESSOR: The NDC code should
be standard across the country,

704
00:38:02,300 --> 00:38:05,120
because those are
FDA assigned codes.

705
00:38:05,120 --> 00:38:08,810
But not every hospital
uses them, OK?

706
00:38:08,810 --> 00:38:10,880
And for the ones
that say zero, I'm

707
00:38:10,880 --> 00:38:13,490
not sure why they're
not associated

708
00:38:13,490 --> 00:38:18,220
with a code in this
hospital's database.

709
00:38:18,220 --> 00:38:26,990
OK, next most common,
you see normal saline,

710
00:38:26,990 --> 00:38:29,570
0.9 percent sodium chloride.

711
00:38:29,570 --> 00:38:32,570
So that was the same stuff
as the flush solution

712
00:38:32,570 --> 00:38:35,450
but this time not
being used for flush.

713
00:38:35,450 --> 00:38:38,270
Metoprolol is a beta blocker.

714
00:38:38,270 --> 00:38:43,760
Here's another insulin this time
with an NDC code, et cetera.

715
00:38:43,760 --> 00:38:48,410
I love bag and vial, OK?

716
00:38:48,410 --> 00:38:51,680
So these are not
